
# Docker — Complete Concepts, Commands & Hands-on Documentation

## 1. Docker Components

### Main Docker components

| Component        | Purpose                                                                  |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Docker Client    | CLI used to send commands to Docker                                      |
| Docker Daemon    | Background service that manages images, containers, networks and volumes |
| Docker Engine    | Docker's container runtime/platform                                      |
| Docker Image     | Read-only template used to create containers                             |
| Docker Container | Running/isolated instance of an image                                    |
| Docker Registry  | Stores and distributes Docker images                                     |
| Docker Hub       | Docker's public cloud registry                                           |
| Dockerfile       | Instructions used to build an image                                      |
| Docker Compose   | Defines and runs multi-container applications                            |
| Docker Swarm     | Docker's built-in container orchestration mode                           |
| Docker Network   | Allows containers/services to communicate                                |
| Docker Volume    | Persistent storage managed by Docker                                     |

