# 29. Override Container Command

Suppose Dockerfile contains:

```dockerfile
CMD ["python", "app.py"]
```

Normal:

```bash
docker run myimage
```

runs:

```text
python app.py
```

Override:

```bash
docker run myimage python test.py
```

Now:

```text
python test.py
```

is executed instead.

This is different from `docker exec`.

```text
docker run image command
    → starts a NEW container with another command

docker exec container command
    → executes another command INSIDE an existing running container
```

