# 31. Docker Volumes

Volumes are Docker-managed persistent storage.

Basic commands:

```bash
docker volume create myvolume
docker volume ls
docker volume inspect myvolume
docker volume rm myvolume
docker volume prune
```

Official Docker documentation recommends volumes for persistent container data because the data exists independently of a container's writable layer.

