# 39. User-defined Bridge Network

Create:

```bash
docker network create mynetwork
```

Run containers:

```bash
docker run -d --name app1 --network mynetwork nginx
docker run -d --name app2 --network mynetwork nginx
```

Now containers on the same user-defined network can communicate using container names.

For example:

```bash
docker exec app1 ping app2
```

User-defined bridge networks provide Docker's embedded DNS-based name resolution.

