# 46. GitHub Actions + Docker Hub

Typical CI/CD flow:

```text
GitHub repository
       |
       | push
       v
GitHub Actions
       |
       +-- checkout code
       |
       +-- Docker login
       |
       +-- Docker build
       |
       +-- Docker test
       |
       +-- Docker push
       v
Docker Hub
```

Docker officially provides GitHub Actions for:

```text
Docker Login
Docker Setup Buildx
Docker Metadata
Docker Build and Push
Docker Setup QEMU
Docker Setup Compose
Docker Scout
```

Typical workflow:

```yaml
name: Docker CI/CD

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main

jobs:
  docker:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Login to Docker Hub
        uses: docker/login-action@v4
        with:
          username: ${{ vars.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME }}
          password: ${{ secrets.DOCKERHUB_TOKEN }}

      - name: Build and Push
        uses: docker/build-push-action@v7
        with:
          context: .
          push: true
          tags: USERNAME/myapp:latest
```

Important:

```text
DO NOT put Docker Hub passwords directly in workflow YAML.
```

Use GitHub Secrets/Variables.

