# 48. Jenkins + Docker

Jenkins can interact with Docker from a Jenkinsfile.

Typical pipeline:

```text
Developer
    |
    v
GitHub
    |
    v
Jenkins
    |
    +-- Checkout
    |
    +-- Build
    |
    +-- Test
    |
    +-- Docker build
    |
    +-- Docker login
    |
    +-- Docker push
    v
Docker Hub
```

Example:

```groovy
pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {

        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                checkout scm
            }
        }

        stage('Build Image') {
            steps {
                bat 'docker build -t USERNAME/myapp:latest .'
            }
        }

        stage('Test') {
            steps {
                bat 'docker run --rm USERNAME/myapp:latest'
            }
        }

        stage('Push') {
            steps {
                bat 'docker push USERNAME/myapp:latest'
            }
        }
    }
}
```

For secure credentials, Jenkins credentials should be used instead of putting passwords directly into the Jenkinsfile.

Jenkins also supports Docker Pipeline functionality such as:

```groovy
agent {
    docker {
        image 'python:3.12'
    }
}
```

and:

```groovy
docker.image('python:3.12').inside {
    sh 'python --version'
}
```

